message: "If you use this publication, please cite it as below."
title: "Hexes, Heresy & Hitmarkers: A Whiteroom Static-Recompilation Evidence Study"
type: report
authors:
  - family-names: Rineer
    given-names: William F.
    name-suffix: III
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
repository-code: "https://github.com/BillTheHuman/hexes-heresy-hitmarkers"
url: "https://github.com/BillTheHuman/hexes-heresy-hitmarkers"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >-
  A non-playable, first-party and AI-assisted evidence study documenting a
  private Nintendo 64 static-recompilation implementation through bounded
  claims, sanitized records, retained negative results, and public verification
  tools. The underlying implementation and game content are not distributed.
keywords:
  - static recompilation
  - reverse engineering
  - software preservation
  - reproducible research
  - evidence verification
